% BibTeX discipline (see docs/publishing-a-paper-2026.md section 1.4):
%   - always include a `url` or `doi` field
%   - inproceedings for conference papers, article for journals,
%     misc with howpublished={\url{...}} for arXiv preprints
%   - keep this file in version control alongside main.tex; arXiv processes
%     .bib -> .bbl automatically (2025 update)
%
% IMPORTANT BibTeX gotcha: BibTeX has no inline comments and it scans the whole
% file for an at-sign followed by an entry type. So a comment must never contain
% an at-sign immediately followed by an entry-type word --- it would be parsed
% as a (broken) entry. Every "TODO verify" note below sits in its own block
% ABOVE the entry it concerns, never on a field line.
%
% Entries with a "TODO verify" note have a field (year / venue / arXiv id /
% page numbers) that should be checked against the canonical source before
% submission. Citation KEYS are stable; only the flagged metadata needs
% confirmation. Do not trust the flagged values blindly.
%==============================================================================


